WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.523
This is the story about
a forgotten genius,

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.863
a gifted sculptor, artist, and
modern-day Leonardo da Vinci,

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.010
whose UFO-like invention was the realm

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.553
of pure science fiction.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.780
But it's also a story about this man,

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.663
his fixation with the past,
and living on borrowed time.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.690
A couple of years ago I got this email

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.450
from a guy named Randy
Hunter, who was promising

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.083
me the greatest nonfiction
story never told.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.210
It was about this
inventor, who lived here,

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.053
in the outskirts of Silicon Valley.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.110
He had done all sorts of amazing things,

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.960
but he'd been forgotten by history,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.640
and for one reason or another,

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.640
I bit on this email, and
for the last two years,

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:23.433
I've been coming to this
guy, Randy Hunter's, place,

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.700
where he has built a temple to

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.553
his obsession, which is this inventor.

00:01:36.109 --> 00:01:38.430
What are you doing in here, man?

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.963
I got another big batch of photos.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:44.170
You got a few minutes to look at this?

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.003
Yeah.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.983
Meet Randy, a successful art
dealer and fine art collector.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.240
And this is the guy he wants everyone

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.383
to know about, Alexander Weygers.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:09.363
Weygers was born in 1901,
in the Dutch East Indies.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.363
As a teen, he moved to
Europe to study engineering,

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.663
and then moved to the
US to study sculpting.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:20.640
Near the end of World
War II, Weygers settled

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.110
in Carmel, California, and it's here

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.400
he carved out a most unusual life.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.170
He built a house made entirely

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.270
from recycled materials,
and objects crafted

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.303
by hand in his blacksmith studio.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.490
Weygers' ability to live off objects

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.703
that other people threw away
turned him into a cult figure.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.730
Youngsters traveled from around the world

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.313
to take his tool making
and sculpting classes.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.550
They also came to marvel at his art.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.423
This is probably the most
photographed Weygers, so far.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.603
Randy discovered Weygers in 2008,

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.183
when for the first time, his
sculptures were put on sale.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.630
Randy snapped up the lot.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.360
As an art dealer, he had dreamed

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.200
of hitting it big by
finding an unknown artist

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.140
and making him famous, and
figured that Weygers was his man.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:19.113
This sculpture's my favorite one.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.420
But what started as a business deal turned

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.193
into a life-altering passion.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.600
Over the next 10 years,
Randy spent countless hours,

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.330
and millions of dollars, tracking

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:33.460
down Weygers' sketches,
personal belongings,

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.210
and all the finished artwork
he could lay his hands on.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.910
He produced a movie about
Weygers, wrote a book

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:42.180
about him, and became convinced

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.403
he discovered a hidden genius.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:51.650
What draws you, what makes
you fascinated about this man?

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.230
I immediately fell in love with him,

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:58.180
because he was just like my style.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.980
I could see the depth
in his work immediately,

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:03.723
and he needed to be
shared with the public.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:11.030
The version of Randy you're
seeing is more sedate

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.773
than the affable, chatty
salesman I first met.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.270
In late 2017, he started

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.170
to lose a multi-year battle with cancer,

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.590
and painkillers made it tough

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:23.653
to get around, and think straight.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.716
You want a hand?

00:04:25.716 --> 00:04:27.053
Sure.

00:04:27.053 --> 00:04:30.300
A few months ago, his cancer came back,

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.810
and as you'll see, he's not at his best,

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.880
he's not the same guy that he used to be,

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.740
and it's a difficult part of the story.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.510
His whole mission has been to make

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:42.180
this Weygers man as famous as he can be,

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.593
and Randy might not get to
see the end of that story.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.230
This is his drawings, blueprints.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.780
Okay, how do you find all this?

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.680
Look at this, man.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.440
This is, all these letters.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.472
Digging, man.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.910
During his hunt into Weygers'
life, Randy discovered

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.230
something extraordinary,
hand-drawn designs

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:14.083
for an exotic aircraft,
dating back to the 1920s.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:19.760
Alex appeared to have invented
the very first flying saucer.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.500
That was an amazing find, in itself.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.810
When I saw the blueprints,

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:27.423
it was undeniable that he was the creator.

00:05:30.058 --> 00:05:30.891
Weygers called his

00:05:30.891 --> 00:05:34.290
futuristic flying machine the Discopter,

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.120
designed to take off vertically,

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.780
and float on a cushion of air.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:40.080
It was a unique concept, and one

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.373
he thought cities of the
future would make full use of.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.220
Weygers patented the Discopter

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.313
in 1944, and then tried to sell it.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.770
He started sending all of these letters

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:58.367
to all kinds of companies,
telling them about his invention.

00:06:03.864 --> 00:06:05.280
As word of the Discopter began

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:09.880
to spread, Alex felt the
US military stole the idea.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.723
It was an accusation they denied,

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.700
but for Weygers, evidence of the theft was

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:18.420
there for all to see, as images

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.760
of his flying saucer seeped
into popular culture,

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:22.980
influencing everything

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.430
from architecture, to cars, and movies.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.510
A two-seater, ready soon, may be the car,

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:29.903
or chopper, of the future.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.670
There's this whole flurry of stories.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:37.250
Weygers First With
"Saucer", a Dutchman says

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.270
he designed flying saucer 23 years ago.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:42.910
The Man Who Invented the Flying Disk.

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:44.910
He didn't really seem
to be after compensation

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:47.900
as much as recognition that
he'd done something important,

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.600
and wanted a bit of credit for it.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:00.263
Spoiler alert, the Discopter
never became a reality.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.290
But the flying saucers it inspired live on

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:10.063
in Randy's collection of UFO memorabilia.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.820
This is the room that I think
of as the ultimate Randy room.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:18.730
This is the tribute to the Discopter.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.400
You've got books, you've got toys,

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.810
everything you could
ever imagine about UFOs.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:27.550
To me, this room has always
represented the heart

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.740
of who Randy is.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.060
He's this guy with a passion that

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:34.150
I think we would all envy, and
hope to have, for something,

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:35.950
but also that bit of his character,

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:38.660
where he can go too
far, and gets obsessed,

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:39.820
to the point where some people,

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.820
I think, would think he's a little nuts.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:46.020
How has your family and friends reacted

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.870
to this, over the years, as
you've gotten deeper into it.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:52.120
Do they think you're a crazed man, or?

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:54.350
How crazy you are, I think, depends on

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.433
how much money you spend on your project.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:05.880
A couple of years ago, Randy,

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.560
and his partner, Cathy, forked

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:11.823
out $1.6 million, for the land
where Weygers used to live.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:18.270
While the original house is
gone, Randy's been busy, turning

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:22.453
his new home into a temple
to all things Weygers.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.780
This is Randy's workshop,
and this is the room

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:29.410
that I think ties him and Alex together.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.850
There's a mix of Randy and Alex's tools,

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.410
and the molds of Weygers' sculptures,

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.973
all lying across the room.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.120
Outside, work has started

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.540
on rebuilding Weygers' artist studio

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:46.370
and blacksmith shop, and there are plans

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:48.780
for a brand-new Weygers museum,

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:52.680
and a UFO fire pit is also in the works.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.290
It'll be shaped like a Discopter,

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.560
and when you're actually burning a fire,

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.670
it would be obvious, from a hundred feet

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:02.653
in the air, that there's a
flying saucer on this property.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:09.810
You might think Randy has
more money than sense,

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:12.200
and let's face it, he hasn't managed

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.530
to make Alexander Weygers and
the Discopter household names.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:17.713
At least not yet.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.790
But in Weygers, Randy discovered
a kindred spirit, a man

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.670
who chose to live by his own rules,

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.943
and who created a legacy,
using his own two hands.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:34.980
What would you say to
Alex if you saw him now?

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.780
I wondered if you had dreamed

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:39.100
about that moment, or anything.

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.950
I did dream about meeting him.

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:42.183
Yeah?

00:09:42.183 --> 00:09:45.570
Figured it was the spirit of Weygers,

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.720
basically telling me I'm
doing the right thing,

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.620
and I should continue with my mission.

